name: Wave 4B — declarative tables (incl. lookup-miss recovery)
description: ```
An unmarked `## Tables` Markdown table defaults to a data binding (a bound
list of records). `the <col> corresponding to the <col> "<key>" in the
table` lowers to a linear lookup that throws `table.lookup_miss` on a miss;
`recover from "table.lookup_miss":` (Phase 5 recovery) catches exactly that
throw via `meridianMatches(_:named:)`.
```
tags: inform7, wave4, tables, codegen

source_inline: ```
---
name: route
---

## Tables
| trigger phrase | skill |
| --- | --- |
| daily briefing | briefing |

## Phases
bind chosen skill = the skill corresponding to the trigger phrase "unknown request" in the table.
recover from "table.lookup_miss":
    complete with reason "no route".
complete with reason "routed".
```

expect_compile: pass
expect_no_unresolved:
expect_workflow_count: 1
expect_workflow_named: Route
expect_swift_contains: state.bind("table", Value.list
expect_swift_contains: throw ToolError.implementation(code: "table.lookup_miss"
expect_swift_contains: catch let _recoveredError where meridianMatches(_recoveredError, named: "table.lookup_miss")
expect_swift_contains: reason: "no route"
